  "q": "Matilda owns a company and wants to expand it by penetrating the Chinese market. She creates an ad and has it translated into Mandarin. However, the ad uses a number of American idioms, so when Chinese viewers see the ad, they get a message that is very different from what Matilda intended. The Chinese viewers are misinterpreting these idioms, causing the ad’s message to fall flat. Which aspect of the communication model is leading to this misinterpretation?",
