  "why": "Seg 11. Feb 23 Lecture 27, part 2, 34:35. Correct Answer: Guerilla Marketing is an innovative, unconventional and low-cost marketing technique aimed at creating a lasting impression and “buzz” for a certain product/brand. Incorrect Answers: Product placement refers to the practice in which products/brands gain exposure for their products by paying for them to be featured in media entertainment such as movies and television shows. Branded Entertainment refers to brand produced content created with the intent to entertain audiences. Sponsorship refers to money that is given to a person or organizational activity to promote a product/brand. Infomercials are television programs that promote a product in an informative and objective way.",
